    "title": "Same Hand, Different Key",
    "summary": "C major and A minor share a window, half their chords, and a note set — so moving between them costs no hand movement, only where you stop.",
    "tags": ["caged", "minor"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
