    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Frets "
        },
        {
          "text": "4–8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " are C major's G form and A minor's E form — the same five frets, the same dots, two names. "
        },
        {
          "text": "One Window, Two Names",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-one-window-two-names"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " proved it. This lesson is what it's for: \"changing key\" sounds like it should mean going somewhere else on the neck. Here it means nothing of the kind."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here are both windows, drawn separately — the diagrams caption themselves "
        },
        {
