          "text": "4–8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and both hold seventeen dots. The dots are in the same places; every label is different. Play the first diagram and you're inside A minor's E form. Play the second and, without moving a finger to a new fret, you're inside C major's G form."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What actually changes is where you stop. In that window C major's "
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "s are "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "3·5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "1·8",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; A minor's "
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "s are "
        },
        {
          "text": "6·5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "4·7",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
