    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That's not a defect to hide. Rotating a loop moves the key without settling it — exactly the honest limit "
        },
        {
          "text": "Same Notes, Different Home",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-what-decides-home"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " already printed: a bare scale run or a two-chord loop can be genuinely ambiguous. A four-chord loop can be too. Real music settles the question with time, repetition and where the phrase actually stops — the engine is being honest about a real limit, not failing at its job."
        }
      ]
    },
